  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Akhtar Ansari vs The State Of Jharkhand ... Opposite ... on 22 February, 2018 Author: Ananda Sen Bench: Ananda Sen In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi B.A. 1002 of 2018 ---- Akhtar Ansari ... Petitioner -versus- The State of Jharkhand ... Opposite Party ---- Coram : Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Ananda Sen ---- For the Petitioner : Mr. Ajay Kumar Sah, Advocate For the State : A.P.P.",
    "facts": "Petitioner is an accused for allegedly committing an offence punishable under Sections 11(a)(d)(e)(i) & (k) of Prevention of Cruelty to Animals Act, 1960, Rule 3 of the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals (Slaughter House) Rules, 2001, Section 55 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and Sections 429, 406, 188 and 120B of the Indian Penal Code. Some camels were entrusted to this petitioner before Bakrid, which were not produced by this petitioner at later stage. It was presumed that this petitioner and others have slaughtered the said animals.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the petitioner is absolutely innocent and has not committed any offence.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the petitioner is absolutely innocent and has not committed any offence.",
